/security-review — loop U10, round 1, range 9476e49..cf07225 (run against the worktree through a sub-task; the engine's own prefill read the main checkout, which has no delta)

No high-confidence vulnerabilities found.

Dropped: repo/tools/mise/tasks/setup-worktree.py.tmpl:73-93 — member names, labels and member_folders are rendered raw into Python string literals, and worktree_install is run through `bash -c`. All of these come from the user's own repo.toml. worktree_install is a trusted command by design (D19). The old shell template already interpolated the same values raw into bash, so the risk isn't new, and the Python version now quotes worktree_install with strings.Quote.
Dropped: repo/tools/mise/tasks/setup-configs.py.tmpl:84-101 and repo/tools/mise/tasks/setup.py.tmpl:82 — member names reach the generated `#USAGE` flags and the env-var names, and the member folder is joined as `{root}/{folder}`. The values come from the user's own values file, every subprocess call uses an argv list with no shell, and member names are re-checked against `[A-Za-z0-9_-]+`. The old shell behaved the same.
Dropped: repo/tools/git/tasks/git-worktree-create.py:51 and git-worktree-delete.py — the branch name, a CLI argument and so trusted, goes into the worktree path and into git argv lists. This matches the old bash and has no shell.
Dropped: repo/tools/docker/tasks/setup-external-update.py:26 — the stamp file has a predictable name in TMPDIR or /tmp. The old bash used the same path and the same rm/touch.
Dropped: repo/tools/claude/tasks/setup-ai.py:150-200 — plugin names and marketplace sources from tools.toml and engine answers go to `claude` as argv. This is the user's own config, there's no shell, and the old bash version was the same.
Dropped: repo/tools/mise/tasks/code-worktrees.py — the HTML page is generated by worktrees_page.py, which was added in an earlier commit (2de0a75), outside 9476e49..cf07225. code-worktrees.py itself uses only argv subprocess calls.
Dropped: cli/internal/oldform/tasks.go:133 (HeaderCopies) and cli/internal/core/plan.go dropCopies — the removal covers only fixed DispatcherDirs paths below .config/mise/tasks. It requires a regular file with the bootstrap header that the manifest doesn't list, and it skips symlinked paths through Lstat and manifest.Linked. I found no path traversal and no symlink-following delete.
Dropped: the gate tasks (`*-lint-*.py`, `*-format-*.py`) — file lists pass to the tools through NUL-separated xargs or argument files. gate_files drops names with a leading `-` or a line break. There's no shell=True anywhere in the changed code.
